('old city tour + panaromic city tour',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','35',35,'Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'10:00 – Leaving Hotel to Old City   - Old City tour starts from Shamakhi Gates followed by below places (Photo stop):  - Shamakhi Gates – The historic entrance to the Old City, showcasing iconic stone architecture.  - Sculptures of Azim Azimzadeh – Artistic monuments honoring Azerbaijan’s famed satirical painter and graphic artist.  - Caravanserai of Bukhara – A restored medieval inn once used by Silk Road traders for rest and trade.  - Caravanserai of Multani – A traditional guesthouse built for merchants from Multan, reflecting oriental caravan culture.  - Maiden’s Tower – Baku’s mysterious UNESCO-listed tower offering panoramic views of the Old City.  - Bazar Square – A lively historic square once serving as the commercial heart of Icherisheher.  - Miniature Books’ Museum – A unique museum displaying one of the world’s largest collections of tiny books.  - Shirvanshahs’ Palace – A majestic 15th-century royal complex showcasing medieval Azerbaijani architecture.   13:00 – Lunch Break   14:00 – Evening City Tour starts with panoramic full evening city view of Baku followed by:   - Highland Park (Which is the highest point in the Azerbaijani capital, opening a panoramic view of the city and its bay. The city''s residents and visitors often come here to see a bird''s eye view of Baku, and just have a walk. The Upland Park can be reached by cable railway (funicular) in 7-8 minutes from the boulevard or by climbing up the endless stone stairs.) Flame Towers (The city''s tallest building. The height of 182 m. Flame Towers - consisting of three high-rise buildings in the complex.)   18:00 – Dinner Break (if included)   19:00 –Drop to Hotel   Overnight in Baku',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',35.0),
