('gobustan & sheki',NULL,'Baku','Baku','113',113,'Overnight',NULL,NULL,NULL,'09:00 – Leaving Baku to Gobustan (1 way x 45 mins)  10:00 – Reaching to Gobustan Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.  11:00 – Leaving Gobustan to Sheki (1 way x 4.5 hrs)  13:30 – Lunch Break  15:00 – Check-in to the Hotel                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           16:00 -Visit Church of Kish - Kish is one of the oldest villages in present-day Azerbaijan and is most known for the ancient Church of Saint Elisha from the period of Caucasian Albania. The current structure was built between the 10th–12th centuries. According to scholars, it stands on the original site where St. Elisha founded the first Christian church in the region, making it one of the earliest spiritual centers in the Caucasus.  17:00 – Visit Sheki Fortress - Sheki Fortress was constructed to protect the historic center, which is now recognized as a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The original fortification walls once reached 8 meters in height and 2 meters in thickness, with defensive towers and arched gates. Although parts were destroyed, several sections have been preserved and restored.  17:00 – Explore Sheki Karavansaray - This historic caravanserai served as a secure lodging place for merchants traveling along the Silk Road with their animals and trade goods. Today, it stands as one of the most iconic and culturally significant architectural landmarks in Sheki.  18:00 Traditional Sheki Halva Tasting Experience Sheki’s famous halva — one of the region’s most well-known traditional sweets. It remains a highlight of local cuisine and a must-try specialty for visitors.  18:30 – Dinner break (if included)  19:30 – Drop at the Hotel  Overnight in Sheki',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',113.0),
