('shahdagh - baku panoramic city tour',NULL,'Baku','Baku','71',71,'Day Trip',NULL,NULL,NULL,'09:00 – Leaving Baku to Shahdag (1 way x 3 hrs)   12:00 – Reaching to Shahdag and visit Shahdag Mountains - Shahdag is the highest part of the side ridge in the territory of the Republic of Azerbaijan. It is separated from the Kyzylgaya plateau by the Gusar river valley. composed of sediments of the Jurassic and Cretaceous systems. Its height is up to 4243 meters (Shahdag peak). There are alpine and subalpine meadows, glaciers with an area of more than 1 square km   Discover the wonders of Shahdag, a land of ancient glaciers, majestic valleys, and stunning mountain lakes! Designed with avid outdoor enthusiasts in mind, Shahdag Mountain Resort offers an array of thrilling activities throughout the year. Picture yourself zooming down the slopes, feeling the crisp mountain air on your face as you carve your way through powdery snow. And for those seeking an adrenaline rush of a different kind, don''t miss the Shahdag Coaster, an exhilarating roller coaster that takes you on a wild ride through the breathtaking mountain scenery.   13:00 – Lunch break   16:00 – Leaving Shahdag to Baku   19:00 – Reaching Baku and doing Panoramic night city tour Panoramic City Tour starts with panoramic full city view of Baku followed by:     - Highland Park (Which is the highest point in the Azerbaijani capital,    opening a panoramic view of the city and its bay. The city''s residents   and visitors often come here to see a bird''s eye view of Baku, and    just have a walk. The Upland Park can be reached by cable railway    (funicular) in 7-8 minutes from the boulevard or by climbing up the   endless stone stairs.)     - Flame Towers -The city''s tallest building. The height of 182 m.    Flame Towers - consisting of three high-rise buildings in the complex. 20:00 – Dinner break (if included)   21:00 – Drop to the Hotel  Overnight at Hotel',NULL,NULL,'Guides (O)',47.0),
('gabala',NULL,'Baku','Baku','71',71,'Day Trip',NULL,NULL,NULL,'09:00 – Leaving Baku to Gabala (1 way x 4.5 hrs)  13:00 – Reaching to Gabala  13:30 – Lunch break  14:30 – Visiting Tufandagh Mountains Resort  - Tufandagh is a mountain peak of the Greater Caucasus range, located in the Qusar District of Azerbaijan. With an elevation of 4,191 metres (13,750 ft) above sea level, it third highest mountain in Azerbaijan. Visit to Nohur lake, guests enjoy with Panoramic Nature view (Located about 5 km. east of the Gabala city, the lake is surrounded by the forests and high mountains called Yumru, Goydag and Gulluburun. The lake covers 240 ha in total and has the maximum depth of 24 meters. The Nohur lake has very clear water thanks to the fresh water sources spilt into the lake. Apart from the small seasonal water supply coming from the mountains of Caucasus, Damiraparan and Vandam rivers also flow to the lake.   17:00 – Leaving Gabala to Baku   21:00 – Dinner Break (if included)   22:00 – Drop to the Hotel   Overnight in Baku',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',71.0),
