('gobustan + heydar aliyev centre',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','41',41,'Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'09:00 – Leaving Baku to Gobustan (1 way x 45 mins)   10:00 – Arrive at Gobustan National Park  - Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.  12:00 – Leaving Gobustan to Baku  13:00 – Lunch Break  14:00 –Visit to Heydar Aliyev Center & “I LOVE BAKU” sign Photostop  - If it’s first time of your arrival to Baku, just be aware of that from the bird view you can clearly see the Heydar Aliyev’s   Signature on the Heydar Aliyev’s Center design. It’s a wave-like  building rises from a bed of concrete. Its immobile white walls   look as though they have been frozen mid-ripple. The abstract   architecture is unlike anything else in the capital city. The   Heydar Aliyev Center, which was designed by renowned architect Zaha Hadid.    18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)  19:00 – Drop to the Hotel    Overnight in Baku',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',41.0),
