('gobustan + absheron tour',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','36',36,'Private Transfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'10:00 – Leaving Baku to Absheron (1 way x 30 mins)   10:30 – Visit to Fire Temple (Ateshgah)  - An ancient Zoroastrian site where flames were historically kept burning as part of religious rituals. The temple provides insight into Azerbaijan’s early religious history and Zoroastrian culture. Visitors can explore the site and learn about the traditions of fire worship.   11.30 - Burning Mountains (Yanardag) - A natural gas hillside that has been burning continuously for decades, creating a unique “burning mountain” phenomenon. It is a famous landmark of Azerbaijan, offering visitors spectacular views and a memorable experience of the country’s natural fiery landscape.   12:00 – Leaving Absheron to Baku   12:30 – Lunch Break   13:30 –Leaving from Baku to Gobustan (1 way takes 45 min)   14:30 – Arrive at Gobustan National Park  - Visit Gobustan National Park, a UNESCO World Heritage site known for its ancient petroglyphs, rock formations, and archaeological heritage dating back more than 40,000 years. The open-air museum offers insights into prehistoric human life, hunting traditions, and early settlements. After exploring the site, continue to the nearby Mud Volcanoes—one of the largest mud volcano fields in the world. The unique grey, lunar-like landscape and constantly bubbling mud pools create an unforgettable natural experience and an excellent spot for photos.   17:00 - Leaving Gobustan to Baku    18:00 – Dinner Break (if includes)   19:00 – Drop to the Hotel    Overnight in Baku',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',36.0),
