('panaromic city tour + heydar aliyev centre',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','35',35,'PrivateTransfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Panoramic City Tour starts with panoramic full evening city view of Baku followed by:      -Highland Park (Which is the highest point in the Azerbaijani capital,    opening a panoramic view of the city and its bay. The city''s residents   and visitors often come here to see a bird''s eye view of Baku, and    just have a walk. The Upland Park can be reached by cable railway    (funicular) in 7-8 minutes from the boulevard or by climbing up the   endless stone stairs.)      -Flame Towers (The city''s tallest building. The height of 182 m.    Flame Towers - consisting of three high-rise buildings in the complex.) + Visit to Heydar Aliyev Center for PHOTO SHOOTING    & â$œI LOVE BAKUâ$ sign for PHOTOSTOP (entry to Vintage Car Museums)   (If itâ$™s first time of your arrival to Baku, just be aware of    that from the bird view you can clearly see the Heydar    Aliyevâ$™s Signature on the Heydar Aliyevâ$™s Center design.    Itâ$™s a wave-like building rises from a bed of concrete.   Its immobile white walls look as though they have been    frozen mid-ripple. The abstract architecture is unlike anything    else in the capital city. The Heydar Aliyev Center, which was    designed by renowned architect Zaha Hadid.)',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',35.0),
