('panaromic city tour + shooting range',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','35',35,'PrivateTransfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Panoramic City Tour starts with panoramic full evening city view of Baku followed by:      -Highland Park (Which is the highest point in the Azerbaijani capital,    opening a panoramic view of the city and its bay. The city''s residents   and visitors often come here to see a bird''s eye view of Baku, and    just have a walk. The Upland Park can be reached by cable railway    (funicular) in 7-8 minutes from the boulevard or by climbing up the   endless stone stairs.)      -Flame Towers (The city''s tallest building. The height of 182 m.    Flame Towers - consisting of three high-rise buildings in the complex.) + Shooting starts with Baku shooting center. Riffle shooting 10 bullets PP (ENTRANCE)    At Baku Shooting Center, which is one of Europe''s    largest shooting complexes, you can practice your    shooting skills, learn how to hit the bull''s eye while    having a blast. With a modern bright interior, the center   hosts many competitions and training both in indoor and   outdoor shooting ranges.',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',35.0),
