('1 day baku city tour',NULL,'Hotel','Hotel','35',35,'PrivateTransfer',NULL,NULL,NULL,'Nizami Street in Baku is an absolute must-visit! The vibrant atmosphere, beautifully lit streets, and a mix of modern and historic architecture create an unforgettable experience. Itâ$™s perfect for a leisurely stroll, shopping at high-end boutiques, or enjoying a meal at one of the many cafes and restaurants. The street truly comes alive in the evening, with its lively vibe and gorgeous lighting. Whether youâ$™re a tourist or a local, Nizami Street offers something for everyone. +                  Old City tour starts from Shamakhi Gates followed by Old city below places (Photo stop) -Shamakhi Gates -Sculptures of Azim Azimzadehâ$™s -Caravanserai of Bukhara -Caravanserai of Multani -Maidenâ$™s Tower -Bazar Square -Miniature Booksâ$™ Museum -Shirvanshahsâ$™ Palace + Walking tour starts along the Baku Boulevard followed by: -Mini Venice of Baku   -Carpet Museum -Deniz Mall    -Ferries Wheel ride    -Carpet Museums   -Boat cruise    -Cristal Hall   -Biking Area       +     Visit to Heydar Aliyev Center for PHOTO SHOOTING    & â$œI LOVE BAKUâ$ sign for PHOTOSTOP   (If itâ$™s first time of your arrival to Baku, just be aware of    that from the bird view you can clearly see the Heydar    Aliyevâ$™s Signature on the Heydar Aliyevâ$™s Center design.    Itâ$™s a wave-like building rises from a bed of concrete.   Its immobile white walls look as though they have been    frozen mid-ripple. The abstract architecture is unlike anything    else in the capital city. The Heydar Aliyev Center, which was    designed by renowned architect Zaha Hadid.)',NULL,NULL,'Sedan - 4 Seaters (Local Speaking)',35.0),
